<title>GERMANY: SKW Trostberg estimates 96 profits up 30pct.</title>
<headline>SKW Trostberg estimates 96 profits up 30pct.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>SKW Trostberg AG said on Monday that it expects 1996 pre-tax earnings to jump by about 30 percent.</p>
<p>Earlier the group reported a 62 percent jump in pre-tax profits in the first half of 1996.</p>
<p>The specialty chemicals group, which earlier announced it planned to buy Master Builders Technologies (MBT) from Swiss group Sandoz AG, reported its first half group pre-tax profit was at 131 million marks.</p>
<p>SKW Trostberg is a unit of utility group Viag AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
